Bitdefender is a cybersecurity leader delivering best-in-class threat prevention, detection, and response solutions worldwide. Guardian over millions of consumer, enterprise, and government environments, Bitdefender is one of the industry’s most trusted experts for eliminating threats, protecting privacy, digital identity and data, and enabling cyber resilience. With deep investments in research and development, Bitdefender Labs discovers hundreds of new threats each minute and validates billions of threat queries daily. The company has pioneered breakthrough innovations in antimalware, IoT security, behavioral analytics, and artificial intelligence and its technology is licensed by more than 180 of the world’s most recognized technology brands. Founded in 2001, Bitdefender has customers in 170+ countries with offices around the world. For more information, visit https://www.bitdefender.com
 About The Role & Team
 We are looking for an experienced DevOps Engineer to join our Data Engineering team as a part of our growing Business Systems, Integration & Data department.
As a DevOps Engineer, you will own the cloud infrastructure, CI/CD and release processes behind our data platform: from the Kubernetes clusters running our data pipelines, analytics and AI services, to the release pipelines of our Salesforce and Microsoft Dynamics 365 environments. You will work closely with data engineers, data scientists, analysts and the business systems teams to keep our services secure, observable and always available.
 Key Responsibilities
Design, build and maintain our infrastructure on Google Cloud Platform (GKE, GCS, BigQuery, IAM, Artifact Registry) using Infrastructure as Code (Terraform);
Deploy, upgrade and operate the services of our data platform on Kubernetes using Helm: Airflow, Apache NiFi, Airbyte, Dremio, dbt, Elasticsearch, relational and non-relational databases and AI/LLM services;
Own and improve our CI/CD pipelines (Bamboo, Bitbucket), container image builds and deployment automation for staging and production environments;
Own the release management process for our Salesforce and Microsoft Dynamics 365 environments: branching strategy, versioning, packaging and deployment of metadata/solutions across sandboxes and production, release planning, rollbacks and release notes;
Define and enforce Git workflows and release practices (branching models, pull request reviews, tagging, release branches) across the team;
Manage secrets, certificates and access: HashiCorp Vault, service accounts, RBAC, SSL/TLS certificates and their automated renewal;
Implement and maintain monitoring, logging and alerting (Prometheus, Grafana, ELK/Filebeat, Sentry, Zabbix) to ensure high availability of our services;
Harden the security of the platform: vulnerability remediation, hardened images, network policies, runtime security (Falco) and least-privilege access;
Own backup and disaster recovery procedures for clusters, databases, buckets and secrets, and keep them tested and documented;
Identify, design and implement internal process improvements: automating manual processes, reducing costs, re-designing infrastructure for greater scalability;
Support data engineers and data scientists with environments, deployments and troubleshooting of production issues.
 Qualifications & Skills
Knowledge of best practices and IT operations in an always-up, always-available service;
Excellent problem solving and troubleshooting skills;
Process oriented with great documentation skills;
Experience with or knowledge of Agile Software Development methodologies;
The ability to work independently and to coordinate releases with multiple stakeholders;
Strong sense of ownership over production systems.
 Must-have
5+ years of experience in a DevOps, SRE or Platform Engineering role;
Strong knowledge of Kubernetes and Helm in production environments;
Strong knowledge of Docker and container image best practices;
Hands-on experience with a public cloud provider (GCP preferred) and with Terraform;
Strong knowledge of Git and release workflows (branching strategies, merging, tagging, versioning);
Experience building and maintaining CI/CD pipelines (Bamboo, Jenkins, GitLab CI, GitHub Actions or similar);
Experience with release management for Salesforce (Salesforce CLI / SFDX, metadata deployments, sandboxes) or Microsoft Dynamics 365 / Power Platform (solutions, environments, deployment pipelines);
Good Linux administration and scripting skills (Bash and Python);
Experience with monitoring and logging stacks (Prometheus, Grafana, ELK or similar);
Experience with secrets management (HashiCorp Vault or similar) and with SSL/TLS certificates.
 Nice-to-have
Previous experience as a software or data engineer (Python, SQL);
Experience with Salesforce DevOps tools (e.g. Copado, Gearset) or Azure DevOps / Power Platform Build Tools;
Experience operating data platform tools: Airflow, Apache NiFi, Airbyte, Dremio or dbt;
Experience with integration platforms such as Workato;
Experience with Kubernetes security tooling (Falco, External Secrets Operator, network policies) and vulnerability scanning (e.g. BlackDuck);
Experience with configuration management tools (Ansible);
Experience deploying and operating AI/LLM services (e.g. Langfuse, vector databases, MCP servers);
A GCP or Kubernetes certification (e.g. Professional Cloud DevOps Engineer, CKA);
A bachelor's degree in Computer Science or a related field.
